/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: A right regular hexagonal prism of base side 30 mm and height 65 mm rests on its base on HP with one base edge parallel to VP. Explain the step-by-step procedure to draw its complete surface development.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Mathematical Pre-Calculations:) Tj
T*
(   - Base Shape: Regular hexagon of side s = 30 mm. Number of lateral faces n = 6.) Tj
T*
(   - Height of Prism: H = 65 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - Length of Stretch-Out Line \(Base Perimeter P\):) Tj
T*
(   P = n * s = 6 * 30 mm = 180.0 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - Lateral surface unfolds into a single rectangle of length 180 mm and height 65 mm!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Step-by-Step Drafting Procedure:) Tj
T*
(   - Step 1 \(Orthographic Elevation & Plan\):) Tj
T*
(   * Draw the top view: A regular hexagon of side 30 mm with one horizontal edge parallel to XY.) Tj
T*
(   * Label vertices 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6 counterclockwise.) Tj
T*
(   * Project front view: A rectangle of width equal to corner-to-corner diagonal \(60 mm\) and) Tj
T*
(   height 65 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 2 \(Draw Stretch-Out Line\):) Tj
T*
(   * Extend the bottom baseline of the front view horizontally to the right.) Tj
T*
(   * Measure a straight distance of 180 mm along this horizontal line \(from point 1 to point 1'\).) Tj
T*
(   - Step 3 \(Subdivide Stretch-Out Line into Panels\):) Tj
T*
(   * Along the 180 mm stretch-out line, mark off 6 equal intervals of length 30 mm each \(points 1,) Tj
T*
(   2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 1\).) Tj
T*
(   * These points represent the unfolded vertical corner edges.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 4 \(Erect Vertical Edge Lines\):) Tj
T*
(   * Extend the top horizontal line of the front view to the right to define the top boundary of) Tj
T*
(   height 65 mm.) Tj
T*
(   * At each marked point on the stretch-out line, erect a vertical line of height 65 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 5 \(Add Top and Bottom Base Covers\):) Tj
T*
(   * To show a complete hollow container development, attach one regular hexagon of side 30 mm to) Tj
T*
(   the top edge of panel 2-3, and one regular hexagon to the bottom edge of panel 2-3.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 6: Darken all outer boundary cut lines with thick continuous lines \(Type A\). Internal) Tj
T*
(   fold lines are drawn as continuous thin lines \(Type B\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 4:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: A right circular cylinder of diameter 50 mm and height 75 mm stands vertically on HP. Detail the step-by-step drafting procedure to develop its lateral surface using the parallel line method.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Mathematical Calculations:) Tj
T*
(   - Base Diameter: D = 50 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - Cylinder Height: H = 75 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - Stretch-Out Line Length \(Circumference of Base Circle C\):) Tj
T*
(   C = pi * D = 3.14159 * 50 mm = 157.08 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - The lateral surface unfolds into a rectangle of length 157.08 mm and height 75.0 mm.) Tj
T*
ET

