T*
(   2. Step-by-Step Construction Procedure:) Tj
T*
(   - Step 1 \(Orthographic Views & Generator Division\):) Tj
T*
(   * Draw top view: A true circle of diameter 50 mm with center O.) Tj
T*
(   * Divide the circle into 12 equal sectors \(30? each\) using a 30-60 set-square.) Tj
T*
(   * Number the division points 1, 2, 3, ... 12 counterclockwise.) Tj
T*
(   * Draw front view: A rectangle 50 mm wide x 75 mm high. Project the 12 generator lines) Tj
T*
(   vertically upward across the front view.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 2 \(Establish Stretch-Out Rectangle\):) Tj
T*
(   * Extend the bottom baseline of the front view horizontally to the right.) Tj
T*
(   * Lay out the stretch-out line of length C = 157.08 mm.) Tj
T*
(   * Extend the top line of the front view horizontally to form a rectangle of 157.08 mm x 75 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 3 \(Subdivide Stretch-Out Line into 12 Generator Spacings\):) Tj
T*
(   * Distance between adjacent generators = C / 12 = 157.08 / 12 = 13.09 mm.) Tj
T*
(   * Divide the 157.08 mm baseline into 12 equal parts using the acute-angle line division method.) Tj
T*
(   * Label divisions 1, 2, 3, ... 12, 1 along the baseline.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 4 \(Draw Generator Lines\):) Tj
T*
(   * From each numbered point on the stretch-out line, erect vertical generator lines to the top) Tj
T*
(   boundary.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 5 \(Add Base Circles for Complete Development\):) Tj
T*
(   * Attach a circle of diameter 50 mm tangent to the top edge at generator 4, and a circle of) Tj
T*
(   diameter 50 mm tangent to the bottom edge at generator 4.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 6: Darken the outer rectangular boundary. Generator lines remain thin construction lines) Tj
T*
(   \(Type B\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
