(>> Solution to Question 5:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: A right circular cone of base diameter 60 mm and altitude 70 mm rests on its base on HP. Derive the sector angle formula and provide complete step-by-step instructions to draw its lateral development.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Mathematical Derivation of Cone Development:) Tj
T*
(   - Base Radius: r = D / 2 = 60 / 2 = 30 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - Vertical Axis Height: H = 70 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - True Slant Height \(Generator Length L\):) Tj
T*
(   L = sqrt\( r^2 + H^2 \) = sqrt\( 30^2 + 70^2 \) = sqrt\( 900 + 4900 \) = sqrt\( 5800 \) = 76.16 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - Geometric Principle:) Tj
T*
(   * When unrolled, the lateral surface forms a circular sector of radius L = 76.16 mm.) Tj
T*
(   * The curved arc length of this sector must equal the circumference of the cone's base circle) Tj
T*
(   \(2 * pi * r\):) Tj
T*
(   Arc Length S = 2 * pi * r.) Tj
T*
(   * On a circle of radius L, the circumference is 2 * pi * L.) Tj
T*
(   * Therefore, the sector angle theta \(in degrees\) is:) Tj
T*
(   theta / 360? = \(Arc Length S\) / \(2 * pi * L\) = \(2 * pi * r\) / \(2 * pi * L\) = r / L.) Tj
T*
(   theta = \(r / L\) * 360 degrees.) Tj
T*
(   - Numerical Computation of Sector Angle theta:) Tj
T*
(   theta = \(30 / 76.16\) * 360? = 0.3939 * 360? = 141.81 degrees \(approx 142?\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Step-by-Step Construction Procedure:) Tj
T*
(   - Step 1: Draw the orthographic front view \(triangle of base 60 mm, height 70 mm\) and top view) Tj
T*
(   \(circle of diameter 60 mm divided into 12 equal sectors\).) Tj
T*
(   - Step 2: At a convenient location on the sheet, select an apex point V.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 3: With center V and compass radius equal to true slant height L = 76.16 mm, swing a) Tj
T*
(   large circular arc.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 4: Draw initial radial line V-1.) Tj
T*
ET

