(>> Solution to Question 6:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: A right regular square pyramid of base side 40 mm and altitude 65 mm rests on its base on HP with base edges equally inclined to VP. Detail the complete procedure to construct its surface development using the radial line method.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Mathematical Pre-Calculations & True Slant Edge:) Tj
T*
(   - Base Shape: Square of side s = 40 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - Vertical Height: H = 65 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - Finding True Length of Corner Slant Edge \(L\):) Tj
T*
(   * In top view, base edges are at 45? to XY. Distance from center O to base corner in plan:) Tj
T*
(   r_corner = s / sqrt\(2\) = 40 / 1.4142 = 28.28 mm.) Tj
T*
(   * In 3D space, true slant edge L is the hypotenuse of height H and plan distance r_corner:) Tj
T*
(   L = sqrt\( H^2 + \(r_corner\)^2 \) = sqrt\( 65^2 + 28.28^2 \) = sqrt\( 4225 + 800 \) = sqrt\( 5025 \) =) Tj
T*
(   70.89 mm.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Step-by-Step Construction Procedure:) Tj
T*
(   - Step 1 \(Orthographic Views\):) Tj
T*
(   * Draw top view: A square of side 40 mm inclined at 45? to XY. Diagonals connect corners 1, 2,) Tj
T*
(   3, 4 to center o.) Tj
T*
(   * In top view, corners 1 and 3 lie on a horizontal line parallel to XY. Therefore, their front) Tj
T*
(   view projection o'1' represents the TRUE LENGTH of the slant edge L = 70.89 mm!) Tj
T*
(   * Draw front view: An isosceles triangle of height 65 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 2 \(Swing Development Arc\):) Tj
T*
(   * Pick a convenient apex point O.) Tj
T*
(   * With center O and compass radius equal to true slant length L = 70.89 mm, swing a large) Tj
T*
(   circular arc.) Tj
T*
(   * Draw initial radial ray O-1.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 3 \(Step Off Base Edge Chords\):) Tj
T*
(   * Set compass or divider strictly to the TRUE BASE EDGE LENGTH s = 40 mm.) Tj
T*
(   * Starting from point 1 on the arc, step off four consecutive chords of length 40 mm:) Tj
T*
(   Point 1 -> Point 2 -> Point 3 -> Point 4 -> Point 1'.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 4 \(Draw Straight Base Edges\):) Tj
T*
(   * Connect points 1-2, 2-3, 3-4, and 4-1' with STRAIGHT LINES \(not circular arcs! The base is a) Tj
T*
(   square\).) Tj
T*
(   - Step 5 \(Draw Fold Lines\):) Tj
T*
(   * Draw straight radial lines connecting apex O to base vertices: O-2, O-3, O-4, and closing) Tj
T*
(   edge O-1'.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 6: Darken boundary cut lines O-1, base segments, and O-1'. Internal radial lines are) Tj
T*
(   drawn as continuous thin fold lines.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
