(   1. Geometric Setup and Mathematical Coordinates:) Tj
T*
(   - Cylinder: Diameter D = 50 mm, Base Radius r = 25 mm, Total Height H = 80 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - Cutting Plane: Inclined at 45? to the base, passing through the axis at height z = 40 mm) Tj
T*
(   \(midpoint\).) Tj
T*
(   - Generator Angles and Heights:) Tj
T*
(   * Divide circle into 12 equal generators at angles alpha_i = 0?, 30?, 60?, ... 360?.) Tj
T*
(   * Height of cutting plane at any generator point x_i = r * cos\(alpha_i\):) Tj
T*
(   Since cutting plane has slope m = tan\(45?\) = 1.0:) Tj
T*
(   z\(alpha\) = 40 + x_i * tan\(45?\) = 40 + 25 * cos\(alpha\).) Tj
T*
(   * Generator Heights:) Tj
T*
(   - Gen 1 \(alpha = 180?, front center\): z1 = 40 - 25 = 15.0 mm \(Minimum height\).) Tj
T*
(   - Gen 2 & 12 \(alpha = 150?, 210?\): z2 = 40 - 25*cos\(30?\) = 40 - 21.65 = 18.35 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - Gen 3 & 11 \(alpha = 120?, 240?\): z3 = 40 - 25*cos\(60?\) = 40 - 12.50 = 27.50 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - Gen 4 & 10 \(alpha = 90?, 270?\): z4 = 40 + 0 = 40.00 mm \(Mid-axis height\).) Tj
T*
(   - Gen 5 & 9 \(alpha = 60?, 300?\): z5 = 40 + 25*cos\(60?\) = 40 + 12.50 = 52.50 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - Gen 6 & 8 \(alpha = 30?, 330?\): z6 = 40 + 25*cos\(30?\) = 40 + 21.65 = 61.65 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - Gen 7 \(alpha = 0?, back center\): z7 = 40 + 25 = 65.00 mm \(Maximum height\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Step-by-Step Development Drafting Procedure:) Tj
T*
(   - Step 1: Draw front view showing the 45? inclined cutting plane line and the 12 vertical) Tj
T*
(   generator lines.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 2: Lay out stretch-out line of length C = pi * 50 = 157.08 mm. Divide into 12 equal) Tj
T*
(   spacings of 13.09 mm labeled 1 to 12 to 1 \(assuming seam is at shortest generator 1\).) Tj
T*
(   - Step 3: From each numbered point on the stretch-out line, project vertical lines upward.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 4: From the front view, project horizontal lines from each cut point on the 45? plane) Tj
T*
(   across to the corresponding generator line on the development:) Tj
T*
(   * Generator 1 & 1': Mark height 15.0 mm.) Tj
T*
(   * Generators 2 & 12: Mark height 18.35 mm.) Tj
T*
(   * Generators 3 & 11: Mark height 27.50 mm.) Tj
T*
(   * Generators 4 & 10: Mark height 40.00 mm.) Tj
T*
(   * Generators 5 & 9: Mark height 52.50 mm.) Tj
T*
(   * Generators 6 & 8: Mark height 61.65 mm.) Tj
T*
(   * Generator 7: Mark height 65.00 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 5: Connect these 13 points with a smooth mathematical curve \(French curve or SPLINE\).) Tj
T*
(   - The top boundary forms a perfect SINUSOIDAL WAVE curve! Darken the bottom line, end edges,) Tj
T*
(   and sinusoidal top curve.) Tj
