(   [Problem Statement]: A right circular cone of base diameter 50 mm and height 60 mm is truncated by an inclined cutting plane at 45 degrees passing through a point on the axis 25 mm above the base. Explain how cut points are transferred to the radial development using true-length generator rotations.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Geometric Parameters & Critical True-Length Rule:) Tj
T*
(   - Base Radius r = 25 mm, Height H = 60 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - Slant Height L = sqrt\(25^2 + 60^2\) = sqrt\(625 + 3600\) = sqrt\(4225\) = 65.0 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - Sector Angle theta = \(r / L\) * 360? = \(25 / 65\) * 360? = 138.46 degrees.) Tj
T*
(   - CRITICAL DESCRIPTIVE GEOMETRY RULE:) Tj
T*
(   * In the front view of a cone, ONLY the two outermost contour generators \(extreme left and) Tj
T*
(   extreme right\) lie parallel to the vertical projection plane and show TRUE LENGTH!) Tj
T*
(   * All interior generators \(e.g. generators 2, 3, 5, 6\) are inclined to VP and appear) Tj
T*
(   FORESHORTENED in front view.) Tj
T*
(   * Therefore, cut points on interior generators CANNOT be measured directly from the apex to) Tj
T*
(   swing arcs!) Tj
T*
(   * They MUST be projected horizontally across to the outer true-length generator first!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Step-by-Step Construction Procedure:) Tj
T*
(   - Step 1: Draw front view showing the 45? cutting plane cutting the 12 generator lines.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 2: From each cut point on interior generators \(points 2', 3', 4'...\), draw a HORIZONTAL) Tj
T*
(   LINE across to the extreme outer generator line o'1'.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 3: Measure the distance from apex o' along the outer generator to each horizontally) Tj
T*
(   projected cut point. These distances are the TRUE DISTANCES from the apex to the cut points!) Tj
T*
(   - Step 4 \(Radial Development\):) Tj
T*
(   * Draw radial sector of radius L = 65 mm and angle theta = 138.5?.) Tj
T*
(   * Divide sector into 12 equal radial generators \(V-1, V-2, ... V-12, V-1'\).) Tj
T*
(   - Step 5 \(Swinging True Length Arcs\):) Tj
T*
(   * With apex V as center and compass radius set to the true distance of cut point 1, swing an) Tj
T*
(   arc cutting radial lines V-1 and V-1'.) Tj
T*
(   * With apex V as center and compass radius set to true distance of cut point 2, swing an arc) Tj
T*
(   cutting radial lines V-2 and V-12.) Tj
T*
(   * Repeat for all 12 cut points.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 6: Connect the plotted points with a smooth French curve. The resulting top contour) Tj
T*
(   forms a smooth non-circular curve bounding the truncated cone development!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

endstream
