(   [Problem Statement]: A transition piece connects a square duct of 60 mm x 60 mm to a circular pipe of 50 mm diameter located centrally at a height of 70 mm. Explain the step-by-step Triangulation Method to construct the pattern for one quadrant.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Symmetry and Quadrant Partitioning:) Tj
T*
(   - The transition piece connects a square base \(60x60 mm at Z = 0\) to a circular top opening) Tj
T*
(   \(diameter 50 mm at Z = 70 mm\) sharing a common vertical center axis.) Tj
T*
(   - The geometry is completely symmetrical about both X and Y axes.) Tj
T*
(   - Therefore, developing ONE QUADRANT \(one-quarter of the total pattern\) is sufficient; the) Tj
T*
(   complete pattern is formed by joining four identical quadrant templates.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Dividing the Geometry into Triangles:) Tj
T*
(   - Consider Quadrant 1 \(Base corner A at \(30, 30, 0\)\):) Tj
T*
(   * The circular top arc in this quadrant spans 90? \(from 0? to 90?\).) Tj
T*
(   * Divide this 90? circular quadrant into 4 equal segments of 22.5? each, labeled points 1, 2,) Tj
T*
(   3, 4, 5.) Tj
T*
(   * Connect base corner A to points 1, 2, 3, 4, 5. This forms four radial triangles: Triangle) Tj
T*
(   A-1-2, Triangle A-2-3, Triangle A-3-4, Triangle A-4-5.) Tj
T*
(   * The flat triangular side facet connecting corner A, adjacent corner B, and point 5 forms) Tj
T*
(   Triangle A-B-5.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. True Length Calculations \(Right-Angled Triangle Method\):) Tj
T*
(   - For every radial seam line connecting base corner A to circular point 'i':) Tj
T*
(   * True Length TL\(A-i\) = sqrt\( \(Plan Length A-i\)^2 + H^2 \) where vertical height H = 70 mm.) Tj
T*
(   * Measure plan distance from A to each point \(1, 2, 3, 4, 5\) directly from top view.) Tj
T*
(   * Calculate true lengths TL\(A-1\), TL\(A-2\), TL\(A-3\), TL\(A-4\), TL\(A-5\).) Tj
T*
(   - Arc chord length 'c' between points on the circle = 2 * r * sin\(22.5? / 2\) = 50 * sin\(11.25?\)) Tj
T*
(   = 9.75 mm.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Step-by-Step Pattern Layout:) Tj
T*
(   - Step 1: Draw line A-1 equal to true length TL\(A-1\).) Tj
T*
(   - Step 2: With center 1 and radius equal to circular chord 9.75 mm, swing an arc. With center A) Tj
T*
(   and radius equal to true length TL\(A-2\), swing an arc intersecting at point 2.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 3: With center 2 and radius 9.75 mm, swing arc; with center A and radius TL\(A-3\),) Tj
T*
(   intersect at point 3.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 4: Repeat to locate points 4 and 5.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 5: Connect points 1-2-3-4-5 with a smooth curve, and connect A to 1 and A to 5 with) Tj
T*
(   straight lines.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 6: Construct the adjacent flat triangle A-B-5 using true base edge 30 mm \(half base\).) Tj
T*
(   This completes the quadrant!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 11:) Tj
T*
