BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the development of a Sphere using the Approximate Methods: the Zone Method \(horizontal latitude slicing\) and the Lune/Gore Method \(vertical meridian slicing\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Non-Developable Nature of Spherical Surfaces:) Tj
T*
(   - A sphere is a doubly-curved surface with constant positive Gaussian curvature \(K = 1 / R^2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Because it curves in two orthogonal directions simultaneously, it is mathematically) Tj
T*
(   IMPOSSIBLE to develop a sphere onto a flat plane without stretching, compressing, or shearing) Tj
T*
(   the material.) Tj
T*
(   - In sheet metal fabrication, spheres are developed using APPROXIMATE METHODS by subdividing) Tj
T*
(   the surface into small segments that approximate single-curved developable surfaces.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. The Zone Method \(Latitude Slicing\):) Tj
T*
ET

