(   - Principle: The sphere is sliced by horizontal cutting planes into a series of horizontal) Tj
T*
(   annular bands called 'Zones'.) Tj
T*
(   - Geometric Approximation:) Tj
T*
(   * Each zone is approximated as a frustum of a right circular cone whose slant surface is) Tj
T*
(   tangent to the sphere along the middle latitude of the zone.) Tj
T*
(   * The top and bottom polar caps are approximated as shallow cones.) Tj
T*
(   - Drafting Procedure:) Tj
T*
(   * In front view, draw tangents to the circular profile at each zone midpoint; extend tangents) Tj
T*
(   to intersect the vertical axis to find the apex of each cone.) Tj
T*
(   * Develop each conical frustum as a curved circular sector of calculated slant height and) Tj
T*
(   sector angle.) Tj
T*
(   * Roll the metal strips and weld horizontally to form the sphere \(common in large spherical gas) Tj
T*
(   storage tanks - Hortonspheres\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. The Lune / Gore Method \(Meridian Slicing\):) Tj
T*
(   - Principle: The sphere is sliced like an orange by vertical meridian planes passing through) Tj
T*
(   the north and south poles into 12 or 24 equal spherical wedges called 'Lunes' or 'Gores'.) Tj
T*
(   - Geometric Approximation:) Tj
T*
(   * Each narrow gore is approximated as a segment of a cylinder whose axis is perpendicular to) Tj
T*
(   the polar axis.) Tj
T*
(   - Drafting Procedure:) Tj
T*
(   * The centerline length of each gore equals the true semi-circumference \(pi * R\).) Tj
T*
(   * The horizontal width at any latitude equals the circumference at that latitude divided by the) Tj
T*
(   number of gores \(w = 2 * pi * R * cos\(lat\) / N\).) Tj
T*
(   * Plot widths along the centerline and connect with smooth curves. \(Standard method for globe) Tj
T*
(   maps and beach balls\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
