(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the Boolean 3D operations in AutoCAD: UNION, SUBTRACT, and INTERSECT, explaining their mathematical set-theory foundation, operational rules, and command syntax.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Set-Theoretic Mathematical Foundation:) Tj
T*
(   - Constructive Solid Geometry \(CSG\) treats 3D solid modeling as a mathematical Boolean algebra) Tj
T*
(   of point sets in three-dimensional Euclidean space R^3:) Tj
T*
(   * Let A and B represent two closed bounded point sets \(solids\) in R^3.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. UNION Command \(UNI - Set Union A U B\):) Tj
T*
(   - Mathematical Operation: Volume = { p in R^3 : p in A OR p in B }.) Tj
T*
(   - Behavior: Fuses two or more overlapping or contiguous solids into a single continuous solid) Tj
T*
(   body.) Tj
T*
(   - Operational Rule: Dissolves and erases all internal dividing boundaries, coincident faces,) Tj
T*
(   and internal voids where solids overlap, leaving a clean unified outer skin.) Tj
T*
(   - Command: UNION [Enter] -> Select solid A and solid B -> [Enter].) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. SUBTRACT Command \(SU - Set Difference A \\ B\):) Tj
T*
(   - Mathematical Operation: Volume = { p in R^3 : p in A AND p NOT in B }.) Tj
T*
(   - Behavior: Cuts and removes the volume of tool solid B from base solid A.) Tj
T*
(   - Operational Rule: Selection order is critical! Base solid \(to keep\) is selected first, Enter) Tj
T*
(   is pressed, then tool solid\(s\) \(to subtract\) are selected.) Tj
T*
(   - Command: SUBTRACT [Enter] -> Select base solid A -> [Enter] -> Select tool solid B ->) Tj
T*
(   [Enter].) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. INTERSECT Command \(IN - Set Intersection A n B\):) Tj
T*
ET

