12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the SLICE command in AutoCAD, detailing all cutting plane options \(3Point, Planar Object, Surface, Z-Axis, View, XY/YZ/ZX\) and the 'Keep both sides' functionality.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Purpose and Architecture of SLICE \(SL\):) Tj
T*
(   - The SLICE command acts as a virtual laser cutter, dividing an existing 3D solid into two) Tj
T*
(   separate solid pieces along a user-specified 3D planar or non-planar cutting boundary.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Command Prompt Sequence:) Tj
T*
(   - Command: SLICE [Enter] -> Select 3D solids to slice -> [Enter].) Tj
T*
(   - Prompt: 'Specify start point of slicing plane or [planar) Tj
T*
(   Object/Surface/Zaxis/View/XY/YZ/ZX/3points] <3points>:') Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Comprehensive Analysis of Slicing Options:) Tj
T*
(   - 3Points \(Default\): Prompts for three non-collinear spatial points defining the cutting plane.) Tj
T*
(   - Planar Object \(PO\): Selects an existing 2D circle, ellipse, closed polyline, or region to) Tj
T*
(   serve as the slicing plane.) Tj
T*
(   - Surface \(S\): Slices a solid using a curved 3D NURBS surface \(allowing organic curved cuts\).) Tj
T*
(   - Z-Axis \(Z\): Prompts for a point on the plane and a second point defining the plane's normal) Tj
T*
(   vector.) Tj
T*
(   - View \(V\): Slices the solid along a plane parallel to the current screen monitor view.) Tj
T*
(   - XY / YZ / ZX Planes: Slices parallel to the principal coordinate planes of the active UCS at) Tj
T*
(   a specified offset point.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Retaining Sliced Halves:) Tj
T*
(   - After defining the plane, AutoCAD prompts: 'Specify a point on desired side or [keep Both) Tj
T*
(   sides] <Both>:':) Tj
T*
(   * Clicking a point on one side of the plane retains only that half, deleting the other half.) Tj
T*
(   * Typing 'B' \(Keep Both sides\) retains BOTH halves as independent, fully functional 3D solids!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
