(   2. Comprehensive Analysis of the 10 Visual Styles:) Tj
T*
(   - 1. 2D Wireframe: Pure vector line and curve display. No surface shading or occlusion. Lowest) Tj
T*
(   GPU resource consumption.) Tj
T*
(   - 2. Wireframe \(3D\): 3D vector wireframe utilizing hardware acceleration, supporting 3D UCS) Tj
T*
(   icons and perspective cameras.) Tj
T*
(   - 3. Hidden: Suppresses and hides all rear edges and surfaces obscured by solid material in the) Tj
T*
(   line of sight \(vector hidden line removal\).) Tj
T*
(   - 4. Conceptual: Warm-cool Gooch shading model. Enhances spatial edge curvature and surface) Tj
T*
(   transitions; favored by mechanical product designers.) Tj
T*
(   - 5. Realistic: Calculates physical material reflectance, ray-traced shadows, and mapped) Tj
T*
(   surface textures \(wood, metal, glass\).) Tj
T*
(   - 6. Shaded: Smooth Gouraud shading with natural lighting.) Tj
T*
(   - 7. Shaded with Edges: Combines smooth surface shading with crisp black vector outlines along) Tj
T*
(   all geometric creases. The undisputed industry standard for 3D CAD modeling.) Tj
T*
(   - 8. Shades of Gray: Monochrome gray shading emphasizing form and lighting without color) Tj
T*
(   distraction.) Tj
T*
(   - 9. Sketchy: Artistic hand-drawn pencil effect with overshooting corner strokes and jittered) Tj
T*
(   lines.) Tj
T*
(   - 10. X-Ray: Semi-transparent shading \(50% opacity\) allowing internal components, bores, and) Tj
T*
(   clearances to be inspected simultaneously without wireframe clutter.) Tj
T*
() Tj
