12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: A truncated right circular cylinder of diameter 60 mm and maximum height 90 mm is cut by an inclined plane such that the minimum height is 30 mm. Provide complete step-by-step drafting instructions to construct its lateral surface development.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Mathematical Pre-Calculations:) Tj
T*
(   - Cylinder Diameter D = 60 mm \(Radius r = 30 mm\).) Tj
T*
(   - Maximum Height H_max = 90 mm \(at rear generator 7\).) Tj
T*
(   - Minimum Height H_min = 30 mm \(at front generator 1\).) Tj
T*
(   - Mean Axis Height H_mid = \(90 + 30\) / 2 = 60 mm \(at generators 4 and 10\).) Tj
T*
(   - Stretch-Out Line Length \(Circumference C\):) Tj
T*
(   C = pi * D = 3.14159 * 60 = 188.50 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - Inclination Angle of Cutting Plane:) Tj
T*
(   tan\(alpha\) = \(H_max - H_min\) / D = \(90 - 30\) / 60 = 60 / 60 = 1.0 => alpha = 45.0 degrees.) Tj
T*
(   - Generator Spacing: C / 12 = 188.50 / 12 = 15.71 mm.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Generator Heights for Development:) Tj
T*
(   - z\(theta\) = 60 + 30 * cos\(theta\):) Tj
T*
(   * Gen 1 & 1' \(theta = 180?\): z = 60 - 30 = 30.0 mm.) Tj
T*
(   * Gen 2 & 12 \(theta = 150?, 210?\): z = 60 - 30*0.866 = 34.02 mm.) Tj
T*
(   * Gen 3 & 11 \(theta = 120?, 240?\): z = 60 - 30*0.500 = 45.00 mm.) Tj
T*
(   * Gen 4 & 10 \(theta = 90?, 270?\): z = 60 + 0 = 60.00 mm.) Tj
T*
(   * Gen 5 & 9 \(theta = 60?, 300?\): z = 60 + 30*0.500 = 75.00 mm.) Tj
T*
(   * Gen 6 & 8 \(theta = 30?, 330?\): z = 60 + 30*0.866 = 85.98 mm.) Tj
T*
(   * Gen 7 \(theta = 0?\): z = 60 + 30 = 90.0 mm.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Step-by-Step Construction Procedure:) Tj
T*
ET

