(   [Problem Statement]: A 90-degree cylindrical pipe elbow of diameter 60 mm connects two horizontal and vertical pipes. Explain the step-by-step layout and nesting of both developable pieces on a single rectangular sheet of metal.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Engineering Principle of the 2-Piece 90-Degree Elbow:) Tj
T*
(   - A 90-degree cylindrical elbow consists of two identical right circular pipe segments cut at) Tj
T*
(   an angle of 45 degrees \(half the turn angle: 90? / 2 = 45?\).) Tj
T*
(   - When the two 45? mitered cylindrical pieces are rotated 180 degrees relative to each other) Tj
T*
(   and welded along their miter seam, they form a perfect 90-degree bend!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Mathematical Symmetry & Nesting Property:) Tj
T*
(   - Let pipe diameter D = 60 mm. Circumference C = pi * 60 = 188.5 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - Let shortest seam height = 20 mm; then longest generator height = 20 + 60 = 80 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - Both pieces have the exact same sinusoidal miter curve.) Tj
T*
(   - NESTING PRINCIPLE: When the second piece is inverted, its sinusoidal curve fits perfectly) Tj
T*
(   into the sinusoidal curve of the first piece with ZERO SCRAP MATERIAL WASTE!) Tj
T*
(   - Total rectangular sheet required: Width = C = 188.5 mm; Total Height = 20 + 80 = 100 mm.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Step-by-Step Fabrication Layout:) Tj
T*
(   - Step 1: Cut a rectangular sheet of metal measuring exactly 188.5 mm in width and 100 mm in) Tj
T*
(   height.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 2: Divide the 188.5 mm width into 12 equal intervals of 15.71 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 3: Plot the sinusoidal miter curve across the center of the sheet using calculated) Tj
T*
(   heights \(from z = 20 mm at ends to z = 80 mm at center generator 7\).) Tj
T*
(   - Step 4: Cut the sheet along this single continuous sinusoidal curve using a CNC plasma or) Tj
T*
(   laser cutter.) Tj
T*
(   - Result: Two perfectly mating elbow segments are produced in a single cut! Roll each into a) Tj
T*
(   cylinder, weld the longitudinal seams, and weld the miter joint.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
