(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the methods of modeling 3D Helical components \(springs and screw threads\) in AutoCAD using the HELIX, SWEEP, and SUBTRACT commands.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   AutoCAD 3D Thread and Spring Modeling Sequence:) Tj
T*
(   1. Generate the 3D Helical Path \(HELIX command\):) Tj
T*
(   - Command: HELIX [Enter]) Tj
T*
(   - Specify center point of base: 0,0,0 [Enter]) Tj
T*
(   - Specify base radius: 20 mm [Enter]) Tj
T*
(   - Specify top radius: 20 mm [Enter] \(Same as base for cylindrical helix\).) Tj
T*
(   - Specify helix height or [Axis endpoint/Turns/turn Height/tWist]:) Tj
T*
(   * Type 'T' \(Turns\) -> Enter number of turns: 6 [Enter].) Tj
T*
(   * Specify helix height: 60 mm [Enter].) Tj
T*
(   - Result: A 3D mathematical spline helix with pitch = 60 / 6 = 10 mm.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Model a Compression Spring \(Circular Wire\):) Tj
T*
(   - Switch UCS to the start point of the helix: Command: UCS -> 3P \(Snap origin to helix start) Tj
T*
(   point; align Z-axis along start tangent\).) Tj
T*
(   - Command: CIRCLE -> Center at origin \(0,0\) -> Radius: 2 mm \(Wire diameter 4 mm\).) Tj
T*
(   - Command: SWEEP [Enter] -> Select 2 mm circle -> [Enter] -> Select the helix path!) Tj
T*
(   - Result: AutoCAD sweeps the wire profile along the 3D coil, creating a solid 3D spring!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Model External Screw Threads on a Bolt \(V-Thread Cutting\):) Tj
T*
(   - Model bolt solid cylinder: CYLINDER of diameter 20 mm and height 60 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - Generate HELIX on cylinder surface: Radius 10 mm, Pitch 2.5 mm, Height 40 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - Draw 2D ISO 60? triangular thread profile at helix start point.) Tj
T*
(   - Command: SWEEP -> Sweep triangular profile along helix path to form a 3D helical thread) Tj
T*
(   cutting ribbon.) Tj
T*
(   - Command: SUBTRACT -> Select bolt cylinder -> [Enter] -> Select helical swept solid ->) Tj
T*
(   [Enter].) Tj
T*
(   - Result: Perfect 3D helical screw threads cut into the bolt shank!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
