/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: A truncated right circular cone has lower base diameter 70 mm, upper base diameter 35 mm, and slant height 50 mm. Calculate the complete cone dimensions and provide the drafting procedure for its lateral development.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Mathematical Calculations via Similar Triangles:) Tj
T*
(   - Frustum Parameters: Lower radius R = 35 mm, Upper radius r = 17.5 mm, Frustum slant height s) Tj
T*
(   = 50 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - Let L be the true slant height of the complete un-truncated cone from apex to lower base.) Tj
T*
(   - By similar right triangles:) Tj
T*
(   r / R = \(L - s\) / L) Tj
T*
(   17.5 / 35 = \(L - 50\) / L => 0.5 = \(L - 50\) / L) Tj
T*
(   0.5 * L = L - 50 => 0.5 * L = 50 => L = 100.0 mm!) Tj
T*
(   - Full Slant Height L = 100 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - Slant distance from apex to top cut face: L_top = L - s = 100 - 50 = 50.0 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - Sector Angle theta:) Tj
T*
(   theta = \(Base Radius R / Full Slant Height L\) * 360 degrees) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
