12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the methods of creating 3D Solids by LOFT in AutoCAD, detailing cross-section alignment, guide curves, path selection, and smooth-fit continuity settings.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Concept of 3D Lofting:) Tj
T*
(   - The LOFT command creates a 3D solid or surface by morphing smoothly through a space series of) Tj
T*
(   two or more planar cross-sectional profiles \(e.g. square base transitioning into a circular) Tj
T*
(   neck\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Input Geometry Rules:) Tj
T*
(   - Profiles must be closed 2D curves \(Circles, Ellipses, closed Polylines, Regions\).) Tj
T*
(   - Profiles can be coplanar or arranged at varying Z-heights or angled planes in space.) Tj
T*
(   - Points can be used as the start or end cross section to terminate in a sharp tip \(e.g. nose) Tj
T*
(   cone\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Lofting Methods:) Tj
T*
(   - Cross Sections Only \(Default\):) Tj
T*
(   * AutoCAD interpolates a smooth cubic surface between the cross-sections.) Tj
T*
(   * Surface Normals option: Controls whether the solid emerges smoothly perpendicular to the) Tj
T*
(   start/end cross sections.) Tj
T*
(   - Guides Option \(G\):) Tj
T*
(   * The user defines one or more longitudinal guide curves \(lines, arcs, splines\) that connect) Tj
T*
(   the perimeters of the cross sections.) Tj
T*
(   * The outer surface of the lofted solid is constrained to adhere strictly to these guide curves) Tj
T*
(   \(critical for aerodynamic fuselages and boat hulls\).) Tj
T*
(   - Path Option \(P\):) Tj
T*
(   * A single central spline curve serves as the spine governing the interpolation path between) Tj
T*
(   cross sections.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Command Sequence:) Tj
T*
(   - Command: LOFT [Enter] -> Click 1st profile -> Click 2nd profile -> Click 3rd profile ->) Tj
T*
(   [Enter].) Tj
T*
(   - Prompt: 'Enter an option [Guides/Path/Cross sections only/Settings] <Cross sections only>:':) Tj
T*
(   * Press Enter or select Guides/Path as required.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
ET

