T*
(   - Opens the Boundary Creation dialog.) Tj
T*
(   - Object Type: Select 'Polyline' or 'Region'.) Tj
T*
(   - Click 'Pick Points' and click inside the enclosed area.) Tj
T*
(   - AutoCAD automatically creates a new, closed polyline perfectly tracing the inner boundary,) Tj
T*
(   leaving original source lines untouched.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. REGION Command \(REG\):) Tj
T*
(   - Command: REGION -> Select all boundary lines/arcs -> [Enter].) Tj
T*
(   - Converts the actual original entities into a 2D planar Region.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Resolving Unclosed Boundary Errors:) Tj
T*
(   - If AutoCAD displays: '0 loops extracted. 0 regions created':) Tj
T*
(   * Cause: The linework has an open gap or overlapping crossed lines.) Tj
T*
(   - Diagnostic Protocol:) Tj
T*
(   * Run OVERKILL to delete duplicate overlapping segments.) Tj
T*
(   * Use FILLET with Radius = 0 on all corner intersections to ensure vertices snap perfectly.) Tj
T*
(   * Execute PEDIT -> Multiple -> Join -> set fuzz distance = 0.5 mm to bridge microscopic gaps) Tj
T*
(   automatically.) Tj
T*
(   - Once sealed, apply EXTRUDE to generate a flawless 3D solid!) Tj
T*
() Tj
