(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the FLATSHOT command in AutoCAD, explaining how to capture 2D orthographic and isometric projection blocks from a 3D solid assembly without entering Paper Space.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Purpose of FLATSHOT:) Tj
T*
(   - Captures a flat, two-dimensional vector projection of all visible and hidden 3D solid edges) Tj
T*
(   as seen from the current active viewport camera, placing the resulting 2D drawing as an) Tj
T*
(   independent block directly into Model Space.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Command Execution Steps:) Tj
T*
(   - Step 1: Position the 3D model in the desired viewing orientation:) Tj
T*
(   * For isometric: Click a corner on the ViewCube \(e.g. SW Isometric\).) Tj
T*
(   * For orthographic: Set view to Top, Front, or Right.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 2: Command: FLATSHOT [Enter] opens the Flatshot dialog box.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Configuration Settings in Flatshot Dialog:) Tj
T*
(   - Destination:) Tj
T*
(   * 'Insert as new block': Places the 2D block directly into the current drawing.) Tj
T*
(   * 'Export to a file': Saves the 2D projection as an external .dwg file.) Tj
T*
(   - Foreground Lines \(Visible Outlines\):) Tj
T*
(   * Color: ByLayer \(or Continuous Blue, 0.5 mm\).) Tj
T*
(   * Linetype: Continuous.) Tj
T*
(   - Obscured Lines \(Hidden Features\):) Tj
T*
(   * Check 'Show' checkbox to display internal hidden features.) Tj
T*
(   * Color: Cyan.) Tj
T*
(   * Linetype: HIDDEN \(or DASHED\).) Tj
T*
(   - Check 'Include tangential edges' to display smooth fillet runouts.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 3: Click 'Create'. Pick insertion point on the 2D drawing canvas.) Tj
T*
