(   [Problem Statement]: Summarize the complete engineering quality assurance protocol for validating surface developments and 3D solid models prior to fabrication release.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Engineering Quality Audit Protocol for Surface Development & 3D Modeling:) Tj
T*
(   1. True Length Verification Checklist:) Tj
T*
(   - Confirm that all generator lengths, slant edges, and base perimeters on the development were) Tj
T*
(   measured from TRUE LENGTH views \(never from foreshortened projections\).) Tj
T*
(   - Check that cone sector angles satisfy theta = \(r / L\) * 360? exactly.) Tj
T*
(   - Verify that cylinder stretch-out lines equal pi * D within +/- 0.1 mm.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Seam & Manufacturing Allowances:) Tj
T*
(   - Confirm that lap joints, lock seams, or welding bevel allowances \(typically 3 to 10 mm\) are) Tj
T*
(   added to boundary edges where required.) Tj
T*
(   - Check that fold lines are clearly distinguished from cut lines by distinct layers and) Tj
T*
(   linetypes.) Tj
T*
(   - Verify that bend relief notches are provided at corner intersections to prevent tearing) Tj
T*
(   during press-brake forming.) Tj
T*
